'''Sunstone Valley''' is a desert area that can be found on the [[Atlas|Atlas]] on a northern extension created among it's arrival. It has open world combat, where [[:Category:Enemies|enemies]] roam the land and attack approaching players. Once a player has been defeated, they are prompted to revive in a safezone or spend 1,000 [[Coins|coins]] to receive on the spot of defeat. When an enemy is defeated, there is a possibility that the player will receive a loot drop; clothes, crafting ingredients, recipes, or consumables. Different enemies types will drop different loots, but all enemies will have a chance to drop a small amount of coins.

Inhabitants of Sunstone Valley range from large reptilian humanoids known as [[Manguana|manguanas]], frontier [[Robgoblin|robgoblins]], [[Feathered Drakes|feathered drakes]], [[Rocklar|rocklars]] and Biker [[Dwarves]].
[[File:Welcometossv.jpg|thumb|300px]]
==Selections==
There are selections in the [[Atlas]], with two [[Locations|locations]] that are viewable.

South is [[Sacred Grove]], near the [[Rough Rider Raceway]], where players can encounter.

North is [[Glimmerdeep]], near the [[Rocklar Village]]. Players couldn't travel there because its entrance is blocked by the barrier.

==Sub-Regions==
In Sunstone Valley, it's split into sections.

The first being is [[Pony Vale]], where the [[Mystical Barrier]] is next to another area where [[Sandspear]] is found in, and the water path is on there where you have to swim there.

The last being is the Rocklar Village, where it is near the [[Drakewind Peak]], and the rock bridge is there where you have to walk there.

